import Lesson from '../../layouts/LessonLayout.astro';

const body = `<h1>5.1c — RPG Character Sheet: Build Your Hero</h1>

<div class="activity expand-app">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">Expand Application</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~30 min</span>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h3>Build: CharacterSheet Class</h3>
        <p>Every RPG has a character sheet: name, class, level, HP, MP, and stats. You'll build the Java class that represents one.</p>
        <p>Create a class called <code>CharacterSheet</code>:</p>
        <ol>
            <li>Instance variables (all private):
                <ul>
                    <li><code>String name</code></li>
                    <li><code>String characterClass</code> (Fighter, Wizard, Rogue)</li>
                    <li><code>int level</code></li>
                    <li><code>int hp, maxHp, mp, maxMp</code></li>
                    <li><code>int strength, dexterity, intelligence</code></li>
                </ul>
            </li>
            <li>Constructor: takes <code>name</code> and <code>characterClass</code>. Calculates stats based on class:
                <ul>
                    <li>Fighter: str=16, dex=10, int=8, hp=40, mp=10</li>
                    <li>Wizard: str=8, dex=10, int=16, hp=20, mp=40</li>
                    <li>Rogue: str=10, dex=16, int=10, hp=25, mp=15</li>
                </ul>
            </li>
            <li>Method <code>void printSheet()</code> that displays all stats in a formatted character sheet.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h3>Think: Where Should the Logic Go?</h3>
        <p>You could put the stat-calculation logic in the constructor, or in a separate method. Which makes more sense? What if you later add a "levelUp()" method — where would the new stats be calculated?</p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="resources">
    <h3>Reference Docs</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-05/class-design.html">Writing Classes</a></li>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-05/constructors.html">Constructors</a></li>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-03/boolean-logic.html">Booleans &amp; if Statements</a></li>
    </ul>
</div>`;
